@page "/docs/components/color-picker"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.ColorPicker
<PageTitle>Color Picker - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Color Picker</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="color-picker" />
        </div>
        <p>A color picker built from parts you can use on their own or together, from a single hue slider to a full panel with gradients, images, swatches and an eye dropper. It reads and writes ten color formats, and when gradients or images are on, its value is the CSS paint for the active surface. Dragging needs an interactive render mode.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ColorPickerUsageExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Alpha"
          Description="`ShowAlpha` adds a transparency slider and includes alpha in the value, which is written in the rgb format here."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerAlphaExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Formats"
          Description="`Format` accepts HEX, RGB, RGBA, HSL, HSLA, HSB, HWB, CMYK, OKLCH and OKLab. Hex shows a free-text field that accepts and converts any format, even without the #, while every other format shows one numeric field per channel. Those channel fields are also how keyboard and screen reader users enter an exact color."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerFormatsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Format dropdown"
          Description="`ShowFormatPicker` adds a format dropdown. Switching it converts the current value into the chosen format and raises the change, and you can bind `Format` to follow along."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerFormatPickerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Saved colors"
          Description="`ShowSaved` adds a panel of saved colors. The plus button saves the current color, clicking a swatch applies it and its corner x removes it. Bind `SavedColors` to persist the list."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerSavedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sizes" Description="`Size` has three width presets. For any other width, pass your own width utilities through `Class`." Example="typeof(ColorPickerSizesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom cursors"
          Description="The draggable surfaces use the OS grab and grabbing cursors by default. `Cursor` and `GrabbingCursor` take any CSS cursor value, and `BzCursor.From` turns a Blaizio icon into one. Set them once on the picker and the area, the sliders and the gradient stop bar all use them."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerCursorsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Swatches"
          Description="Preset colors as one-click swatches. The swatch that matches the current color shows as selected."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerSwatchesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Surfaces"
          Description="Turn on `ShowSolid`, `ShowGradient` and `ShowImage` to offer those surfaces, and a switch appears once more than one is on. `Value` is the CSS paint for the active surface: a color, a gradient, or `url(...)` for an image. Bind `Gradient` and `Image` when you need the structured models behind those strings."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerSurfacesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Palette"
          Description="`BzColorPalette` lays presets out as named ramps, with a label per row and the shades lined up column by column. Pass `Groups`, or compose `BzColorPaletteGroup` children."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerPaletteExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Composed"
          Description="Put the parts in `ChildContent` to build your own layout, from a minimal area and hue pair to a full panel."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerComposedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Minimal"
          Description="Two parts and nothing else. The root holds the color, so any subset of the parts is a working picker."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerMinimalExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Hue only"
          Description="The same idea taken further: a single hue slider drives the whole color."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerHueOnlyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Opacity only"
          Description="A fixed color where only the transparency can change, using the alpha slider and its numeric field."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerOpacityOnlyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="In a popover"
          Description="A swatch button that opens the picker. The trigger is rendered with `RenderAs` and the picker sits inside `BzPopoverContent`."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerPopoverExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Eye dropper"
          Description="`ShowEyeDropper` adds the browser's native eye dropper, in browsers that support it."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerEyeDropperExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Commit"
          Description="`ValueChanged` fires on every pointer move, while `OnValueCommit` fires once when an interaction settles. Save the color in `OnValueCommit`."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerCommitExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Live preview" Description="Bind the picked color straight into an inline style to preview it live." Example="typeof(ColorPickerLiveExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Example="typeof(ColorPickerDisabledExample)" />
</div>
